nodecode-harnmem is a rewrite of ys118's ys118/harnmem:

  https://github.com/ys118/harnmem
  commit 20c644ef4276284494519ed96305bb371ff05dc3
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 HarnMem contributors (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is packages/hermes-harnmem of that commit. Its two halves
are carried over: the injection (a small, byte-stable snapshot at the head of a
turn's context, cached so two turns without a write carry the same bytes) and
the five tools (harnmem_search, harnmem_write, harnmem_read, harnmem_forget,
harnmem_status), with the original's names, descriptions, parameters and JSON
answers, and with a write with an existing active title merging into it. The
engine the plugin drove through a Node child process is rewritten in Lisp: the
store's layout (memories/user and memories/projects/<project>, one Markdown
file per memory, the original's YAML frontmatter subset, state/, trash/,
VERSION), its four memory types and its statuses, the lexical ranker, the
hot-index score (importance, confidence, recency, use, pinned) and the budgeted
snapshot layout with its header and footer. A memory written by this cell is
read by the other HarnMem harnesses, and theirs by this cell.

What was left out, and why: the session-end extraction pass, because it needs
an OpenAI-compatible endpoint and a model call the original only makes when
auto_extract is turned on -- the model writes its own memories with
harnmem_write here, which is the path the original also keeps working with no
endpoint at all; the JSON search index (index/<shard>.json) and the per-shard
MEMORY.md, which this cell leaves to the engine's own rebuild while it reads the
Markdown files directly; the original's skip/merge/supersede dedupe decisions
and validity windows, replaced by a merge on an existing active title; the
digests and the consolidation pass; and the `hermes harnmem status|search|read`
CLI, whose answers the config section, /settings and /harnmem give. The
plugin's Python provider and its Node bridge are not bundled: a cell carries
neither. LICENSE is the plugin's repository LICENSE, unchanged.
